+| D46 | Where the development engine runs (Stage 5 step 1) | Render free; Render paid; Azure | **Render Blueprint (`render.yaml`), free web service + free Postgres 16, Frankfurt, no Redis (jobs in-process).** Free has no pre-deploy command, so `engine/scripts/start.sh` runs `alembic upgrade head` then uvicorn on `$PORT`; `ENVIRONMENT=development` (the only mode that seeds default rules and watched sources at start-up). `postgres://` / `postgresql://` URLs are normalised to `postgresql+psycopg://` (psycopg 3; psycopg2 is not installed). ALLOWED_ORIGINS drops a trailing `/`. Storage is the container disk (ephemeral: lost on restart, redeploy or sleep); database expires after 30 days. Weekly FTA monitor cron left commented out (cron has no free plan; it would not share the web service's files). **Dummy data only** | Change `plan:` in render.yaml (e.g. `0.5c-512mb`); uncomment the cron block; add a disk or object storage before real data |
+| D47 | Who approves a **shared default** (platform user, no firm claim) | TaxPartner or Admin (Stage 3); or the D43 domain split | **D43 split, Admin never**: TaxPartner for tax domains (VAT, INPUT_VAT, CT, TRN, LEGAL_REF), Partner for methodology (SAMPLING, JE, BENFORD, VALIDATION, ...). Same for reject. Supersedes the "Tax Partner or Admin" wording in SPEC 3.8; `APPROVER_ROLES` is now `("TaxPartner", "Partner")` | `FIRM_TAX_APPROVERS` / `FIRM_METHOD_APPROVERS` / `TAX_DOMAINS` in app/services/rules.py |
+| D48 | Where the Supabase firm claim is read | `app_metadata` then top-level (Stage 3 fallback); or `app_metadata` only | **`app_metadata.<AUTH_FIRM_CLAIM>` only** for `AUTH_PROVIDER=supabase` (server-set; a top-level claim could come from a custom hook or a third-party token and is ignored, like `user_metadata`). Entra: top-level claim. `dev` (development only) keeps the fallback, like its roles | app/core/security.py `_principal` |
+| D49 | VARCHAR lengths only failing on PostgreSQL | Shorten seed units; or widen the column | **Migration 0009 widens `rule_versions.unit` to 128** (three JE seed units are 41-64 characters; SQLite never enforced 32). Found by a local PostgreSQL 16 rehearsal of the Render start. The suite can now run on PostgreSQL: set `AUDITSMART_TEST_PG_URL` to a scratch database (its schema is dropped per test) | `alembic downgrade 0008` reverses it (fails if a longer unit is stored) |
